YANI:  New Terrain: Arrow Slit

This is a "wall" with the special property that a normal monster cannot
move into it, but can both see through it and fire missile weapons
(wands, crossbow bolts, darts, arrows) through.

Additional wrinkle:  Give it a "facing" of "inside" and "outside".   A
person firing a weapon from the "inside out" fires as normal. A person
shooting back from the "outside in" suffers, say -4 to hit,
demonstrating that the people inside have the advantages of cover and
concealment.

Where used: Castle towers and walls, which will be manned by soldiers
armed with missile weapons or wands.   In particular,  on the front
wall and in the turrets, so that an adventurer walking up to the gate
faces a three-way crossfire.  If these soldiers are randomly armed with
wands of death or magic missile, it should make his life/her life very
interesting.

This discourages the adventurer from using the location in front of the
castle as a sanctuary area, which it most certainly would not be "in
real life" -- real-life castles were specifically designed to make the
area around them a killing zone swept with archers and siege weapons.
It also allows an additional strategy on the part of the adventurer --
maneuvering so that the archers shoot the eels and sharks in the moat,
rather than the adventurer. 

